  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Rhino &amp; Tiger Conservation Fund</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The purpose of this proposal is to support the law enforcement components of a project to conserve the tiger in the Endau-Rompin landscape. The Recipient will do this by: (1) supporting joint patrols (once a month and up to five days in length), short patrols (up to twice a month and 2 to 5 days in length) and checkpoint operation at road accesses to the northern half of the Johor Endau Rompin landscape; (2) conducting land use ground-truthing and wildlife recce surveys in new forest conversions and habitat bottlenecks in parts of Mersing District; (3) highlighting use of these corridors by wildlife in a report to the Johor Wildlife Conservation Project Steering Committee; and (4) analyzing the current land-use at these vital bottle necks using GPS and GIS mapping.</narrative>
  </description>
